  "source": "microsoft/vscode at commit 9192ec485939d98bb8b81410e03cee0a34747573 (MIT licence, see LICENSE.txt). A theme file only lists the colours it changes; VS Code fills in the rest from these defaults. Dark and light are the 'dark' and 'light' columns of each registerColor call. High contrast themes use the dark and light columns here. An object {of, alpha} is that key at that opacity; {of, lighten} and {of, darken} are VS Code's Color.lighten and Color.darken of that key (HSL lightness moved by that fraction of itself), as button.hoverBackground is written in inputColors.ts.",
